{"skill":{"slug":"mx-macro-data","displayName":"Global Macro Database Assistant"},"version":{"version":"1.0.12","createdAt":1776424761300,"changelog":"Publish 1.0.12","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":13171,"sha256":"2a86e1520737b927ba488f81ace80420f894abc7ebf64df46a563dc5f4843497","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/get_data.py","size":19269,"sha256":"cd3fbc80220df8eb80b95e17395c3eb8f01b40c5eaa1519b1f1956eca1ad2423","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2639,"sha256":"306c6d33331bcc35b0d8e22d2c60d57a9df6d403defcd57ac0230f3db7c865b2","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789173036649,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"7e1af991d4e47e1c73a9c95d42328cb1e80770d3505c94e6c131748c93e08c03","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7e1af991d4e47e1c73a9c95d42328cb1e80770d3505c94e6c131748c93e08c03","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780085990293},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":24,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789173036649},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill appears to do what it says: query Eastmoney macroeconomic data, then save CSV and description files, with some install and CSV-handling cautions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of EM_API_KEY, outbound network access, and output file writes is proportionate to the macro-data retrieval purpose; the key is sent in an API header and is not printed, while the query body is logged.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The install metadata and docs install the third-party httpx package without a pinned version and suggest pip --user, which is a supply-chain and shared-environment hardening gap rather than evidence of malicious behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill includes mandatory orchestration guidance for follow-up completeness checks and up to 5 retry queries; this is disclosed and purpose-related, but users should expect possible extra API calls and quota use.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No autostart, background worker, scheduled task, memory writing, credential store access, deletion, privilege escalation, or cross-session persistence behavior was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, runtime behavior, and code align: it takes a natural-language macroeconomic query, sends it to an Eastmoney API using EM_API_KEY, parses returned tables, and writes CSV plus TXT outputs.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install in an isolated Python environment if possible, set EM_API_KEY only for users and sessions that need this service, and treat generated CSV files as untrusted external data when opening them in Excel or similar spreadsheet software. Expect the skill to contact Eastmoney services and to write result files under the configured output directory.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The environment secret, network call, and file writes are expected for this skill, but the package does not declare tighter tool/path scoping beyond requiring EM_API_KEY.\n[SQP-3] expected: The documentation and examples are mostly Chinese, which fits the Eastmoney macro-data use case; this is a usability/localization note, not a security concern.\n[SQP-3] expected: The script help text and docstring are also Chinese-focused; no hidden behavior or user-control issue was found from this language choice.\n[T09] unexpected: CSV output writes remote API values without spreadsheet formula escaping, so users opening files in spreadsheet apps should treat them as untrusted external data.\n[T08] unexpected: The dependency on httpx is ordinary for HTTP access, but leaving it unpinned reduces reproducibility and supply-chain assurance.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789173036649}}}}}